WS73 USB stop-work producer lifetime
===================================

  python3 tools/testing/ws73/formal/run-tlc.py --jar /path/to/tla2tools.jar

Requires Java and TLC 2.19 revision 5a47802. Uses one worker, 512 MiB Java heap,
a 60-second deadline per exploration and the shared WS73 build lock. TLC's
single-machine state store creates a local RMI socket; a socket-denying sandbox
cannot run it. No distributed workers, physical USB, firmware or kernel are
executed. Check the shared CPU budget first. Inputs must be clean/committed.

The current model checks TypeOK and NoUseAfterFree: after freeing the USB
owner there can be no pending/running stop work or active fault producer.
The old-order configuration must expose the concrete delayed BLE backend
counterexample, not merely fail for any reason. Every command, model/config,
production source listed below, tool version/hash, raw output, reachable state
dump and supervisor control result is saved under ../.dev/ws73-upstream/records.
Timeout, abnormal exit, warning, incomplete statistics, missing terminal states,
wrong invariant and truncated/missing/duplicate result messages cannot pass.

Source mapping (review again if these functions or their callers change):

* Begin: ws73_usb_submit_rx / ws73_usb_io_transfer serialize admission with
  ws->lock. A backend activation represents one admitted ws73_ble_send call
  holding ble->operation through its backend return. The child may be active
  before the initializer returns from auxiliary_device_add.
* Giveback: __usb_hcd_giveback_urb in drivers/usb/core/hcd.c removes the URB
  from its anchor before invoking the callback, with suspend_wakeups held.
  Submitted, active, claimed and enqueued receiver states all prevent join.
* ClaimFault: ws73_usb_fail sets error/first under ws->lock; QueueStop models
  the later schedule_work after platform/startup/BLE aborts without that lock.
  Arbitrary delay between these steps includes preemption, not a sleep under
  the parent spinlock. Only the first fault queues stop.
* Return: completion, initialization or backend returns. Backend return is
  inside ws73_ble_send's operation-mutex critical section. Done includes the
  following unlock; removal must join it before clearing backend/context.
* RunStop/EndStop: ws73_usb_stop joins the anchor plus RX/interrupt URBs.
* Close through Free: ws73_usb_unbind closes admission, aborts requests, joins
  anchor/RX/interrupt, cancels initialization, removes the BLE child, finally
  cancels stop and frees owner buffers/object. ws73_ble_link_remove calls
  ws73_ble_remove, which faults the endpoint, clears backend/context while
  holding operation, deletes/unbinds the auxiliary consumer and uninitializes.
* JoinAnchor: current drivers/usb/core/urb.c usb_kill_anchored_urbs checks
  usb_anchor_check_wakeup, including suspend_wakeups. It ALREADY guarantees
  completer callbacks have finished. Treating an empty list as sufficient
  would misrepresent this kernel. Explicit per-URB joins remain in the model
  and driver, but this model does not claim omitting them causes a callback UAF.

With DrainBackendFirst=FALSE the historical final cancel occurs before child
removal. A backend can claim first fault while admission is open, pause,
resume after that cancellation, queue stop, return, and allow removal/free
with stop still queued. TRUE moves cancellation after all producers join.
This is a source-derived schedule and model counterexample, not a claimed
reproduction of UAF in an executing kernel. The C fix changes the actual
ws73_usb_unbind ordering. The runner checks that ordering as a drift guard;
text matching does not prove equivalence between C and TLA+.

Scope and assumptions
---------------------
One owner, two receiver producers, one initialization and one backend call;
each receiver has at most one submission/giveback and there is at most one
first fault. The state graph is finite and exhaustive for this abstraction,
with no state constraints or simulation mode. No liveness/fairness property
is claimed. Terminal stutter permits completion while keeping deadlock checking
enabled in nonterminal states. The state dump must include actual free states,
preventing a safety pass obtained solely by making teardown unreachable.

Caller object lifetime, lock exclusion, USB join, workqueue cancellation and
auxiliary removal contracts are assumed from the mapped code. Control waits,
URB status/length, resubmission, request stack lifetime, HCI callbacks and
auxiliary reference release are abstracted; aborts do not make arbitrary
callbacks atomic. This is NOT a C concurrency/refinement proof, LKMM analysis,
complete lifecycle model, USB core proof, firmware/epoch qualification or real
hardware result. TLC uses fingerprints; its reported collision estimate is
retained. Broader multi-instance, recovery and PM properties remain open.
